          color="#000000"
        > -->
        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
<h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 500; margin: 0;">
  Golden Dome doubts
</h2></mj-text><mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="REPLACE_ME"
  target="_blank"
  href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="0px 12px 20px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000"><p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 10px 0 0 0;"><strong>What happened? </strong>The US Congressional Budget Office (CBO) says President Trump’s proposed “Golden Dome” missile defense system could <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cqxp27j1xyjo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">cost about $1.2T over 20 years</a>, far above the earlier $175B estimate. The system is designed to protect the US from ballistic, cruise, and next-generation missile threats using land, sea, and space-based technology. However, the CBO warned it may still be overwhelmed by a major attack from Russia or China.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 10px 0 0 0;"><strong>Why? </strong>The Golden Dome may struggle against Russia or China because both have large, advanced missile arsenals designed to overwhelm defense systems. A full-scale attack could involve countless ballistic missiles, cruise missiles, hypersonic weapons, decoys, and drones launched from different directions. Even a highly advanced shield may not track, target, and intercept every threat in time. Space-based sensors and interceptors could also become targets themselves, especially in a conflict with a major power.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 10px 0 0 0;"><strong>Contracts:</strong> SpaceX and Lockheed Martin have secured contracts worth up to $3.2B to develop space-based missile-interceptor prototypes for the Golden Dome system. But the contracts are still for prototypes, not a finished shield. That means major questions remain over expenses, feasibility, reliability, and whether such technology can work at scale against advanced missile attacks from countries like Russia or China.</p></mj-text>
        <!-- </mj-text> -->
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
