            "
          >
            Worldwide
          </h2>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image
          border-radius="10px"
          padding="10px 12px"
          width="600px"
          src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
          alt="REPLACE_ME"
          href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
        />
        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇳🇷 Nauru - Name change. </strong>Nauru will hold a referendum on changing its official name to “Naoero,” after parliament passed a constitutional amendment backing the move. The government says “Nauru” came from foreign mispronunciation of the island’s native name and sees the change as a way to reclaim its heritage, language, and identity. The name Naoero comes from “Dorerin Naoero,” the native language spoken by many citizens alongside English (<a href="https://www.dw.com/en/nauru-change-name-naoero-referendum/a-77140283" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">island identity</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇦🇫 Afghanistan - EU invites members.</strong> The European Commission has invited Taliban representatives to Brussels for talks on deporting Afghan nationals who were refused permission to stay in the EU. Officials said the meeting would be a follow-up to earlier technical talks in Afghanistan and does not mean the EU recognizes Taliban rule. The push came after 20 EU and Schengen countries complained that just 2% of Afghans issued return orders in 2024 were actually sent back (<a href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-invites-taliban-members-to-discuss-afghan-migrant-returns/a-77134268" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">Taliban talks</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇬🇭 Ghana - Evacuates South Africans. </strong>Ghana says it will evacuate 300 citizens from South Africa after a wave of protests and alleged xenophobic attacks targeting foreign nationals. FM Samuel Okudzeto Ablakwa said the Ghanaians had registered with the embassy in Pretoria and would be rescued after a safety advisory. South Africa has denied reports of attacks, saying some viral videos were fake, but President Cyril Ramaphosa acknowledged protests and criminal acts against foreigners (<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cedpv17gqqzo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">embassy rescue</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇺🇲 USA - Defends subpoenas. </strong>Acting US Attorney General Todd Blanche has defended issuing subpoenas to journalists in investigations into leaks of classified information. Blanche said prosecuting leakers who share national secrets with reporters is a priority, arguing such leaks risk national security and soldiers’ lives. President Trump also attacked media coverage of the war, calling some reporting “virtual treason.” Press groups and The Wall Street Journal’s publisher criticized the subpoenas (<a href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260512-us-attorney-general-defends-press-subpoenas-over-classified-leaks" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">press pressure</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
