            Foundations
          </h2>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 500; margin: 0;">
    Why is Switzerland neutral?
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border="1px solid #00000013"
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="REPLACE_ME"
  href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
/>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Status: </strong>Switzerland’s neutrality stems from both history and strategy. After the 1515 <a href="https://www.britannica.com/event/Battle-of-Marignano" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">Battle of Marignano</a>, the Swiss Confederation chose to refrain from foreign wars. This policy was formally recognized in 1815 at the Congress of Vienna, where European powers agreed that a neutral Switzerland would help maintain continental stability. Neutrality preserved unity among Switzerland’s diverse linguistic and religious groups and allowed it to prevent military entanglement.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>On the ground: </strong><a href="https://studyinginswitzerland.com/switzerland-a-neutral-country/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">Switzerland upholds its neutral stance</a> through diplomacy, military readiness, and strict non-alignment. It has a well-trained military to defend its borders if needed. Switzerland refrains from joining military alliances such as NATO. This practical approach has enabled Switzerland to play a distinctive role in global diplomacy by hosting international institutions in Geneva and mediating conflicts worldwide.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Criticisms: </strong>Some critics argue that remaining neutral doesn't take a clear stance on human rights violations, aggression, or breaches of international law. Switzerland was criticized for banking with both sides during the Second World War. Moreover, Switzerland’s neutral stance may be outdated in the current context, especially amid hybrid threats following the Russia-Ukraine war.</p>
</mj-text>
